Mass of protons in the body:

\[
m_p\text{-mass}=\frac{62}{2}=31\ \text{kg}
\]

Number of protons:

\[
N=\frac{31\ \text{kg}}{1.67\times 10^{-27}\ \text{kg}}
\approx 1.86\times 10^{28}
\]

Decay constant:

\[
\lambda=\frac{\ln 2}{T_{1/2}}
=\frac{0.693}{10^{33}\ \text{years}}
\]

Decays per year:

\[
A=\lambda N
=\frac{0.693(1.86\times 10^{28})}{10^{33}}
\approx 1.29\times 10^{-5}\ \text{decays/year}
\]

Decays per day:

\[
\frac{1.29\times 10^{-5}}{365}
\approx 3.5\times 10^{-8}
\]

The answer is (A)

